import json

def add_v14(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture,link,is_glasses):
 O=P/'engineering-v14-results';V13=P/'engineering-v13-results'
 if not (O/'cad_report.json').exists():return
 cad=json.loads((O/'cad_report.json').read_text())
 assembly=json.loads((O/'assembly_path_audit.json').read_text()) if (O/'assembly_path_audit.json').exists() else None
 motion=json.loads((O/'ocp_motion_audit.json').read_text()) if (O/'ocp_motion_audit.json').exists() else None
 step=json.loads((O/'STEP_verification.json').read_text()) if (O/'STEP_verification.json').exists() else None
 new_page(d,'V13 Assembly failure and V14 rear cap')
 para(d,'V13 tried a removable side cap. The first cap also clashed with a screw head; a clearance recess corrected that clash. The later assembly check found a more basic problem: the fixed spring guide obstructed radial insertion. Forty eight of sixty sampled cap or pin withdrawal positions failed. Passing STEP exports did not make this design ready to build. V13 was rejected as an assembly route.')
 para(d,'The recorded V13 motion audit was stopped after this failure. Its saved samples are incomplete and are not a six size motion pass. One adult small inner fork calculation gave about 0.147 mm load direction displacement and 13.58 MPa sampled peak stress under the ideal 11.63 N locking bore load. It has only one mesh, so refinement was not established. Neither result qualifies its cap or screws.')
 para(d,'V14 changes to a rear axial cap and a separate pull knob. The pin and collar enter from the rear. A coil can slide over the bare rod. The cap guide slides along the rod and seats the spring. Two nominal M1.6 by 6 screws and nuts retain each cap. The pull knob attaches last. Actual threads, knob retention, torque, spring ends and assembly tools still need design and qualification.')
 if (P/'documents/images/V14_cap_section.png').exists():picture(d,'V14_cap_section','Sections through saved V14 CAD. Colours identify parts and do not select materials. The exploded offsets explain assembly; they are not a physical assembly trial.',5.8)
 if is_glasses:
  f=O/'fork_mechanics_summary.json'
  if f.exists():
   r=json.loads(f.read_text())['cases'][0]
   para(d,f"The V14 adult small main fork fixture now has two completed meshes. Displacement changed by {100*r['displacement_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent and sampled peak stress by {100*r['sampled_peak_stress_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent. Both are within the chosen 5 percent comparison limit. This is a standalone component calculation, not a Sony pad or complete joint result.")
  para(d,'The newer V14 box calculation makes the child carrying limit clearer: child small shrinks by less than 1 percent, while child medium and large become about 1 to 1.5 percent larger when folded. Adult examples shrink by about 12 to 23 percent. A clear folding path does not prove useful portability.')
  para(d,'These changes belong to the standalone ear defender. They do not alter the Sony WH CH720N or validate its replacement pad. The original pad and mounting groove measurements remain deferred by the user. Its generic V8 cushion is unchanged. No new fit, glasses pressure, incoming noise, outgoing music, response or ANC pass is added.')
  para(d,'Both reports share the same revision and limits. V14 is local STEP work; the newest native Fusion archives remain V10. The main project report contains the detailed new checks and retained failures. Earlier market prices remain a dated comparison, not a new quote or proof that our design is better.')
  return
 new_page(d,'V14 Recorded checks and open work')
 rows=[['Saved candidate sizes',str(len(cad['sizes']))+' of six','Local STEP files with 44 solids per assembly'],['STEP reimport checks',str(step['case_count'])+' and '+('pass' if step['all_pass'] else 'fail') if step else 'Not completed','Counts and volumes only'],['Assembly path samples',str(assembly['case_count'])+' and '+('pass' if assembly['all_pass'] else 'fail') if assembly else 'Not completed','Discrete rigid cap and pin movement'],['Adjustment release and folding',str(motion['case_count'])+' and '+('pass' if motion['all_pass'] else ('incomplete' if motion['case_count']<216 else 'fail')) if motion else 'Not completed','No continuous or loaded contact proof'],['New fork structural fixture','Recorded below' if (O/'fork_mechanics_summary.json').exists() else 'Not completed','V12 and V13 fork stresses cannot qualify V14'],['Final complete joint contact','Not completed','Pin bearing cap screws knob threads torque friction and stops'],['Comfort heat and sensory acceptance','Not physically tested','Measured materials and voluntary wearer trials'],['Noise reduction and music leakage','Not physically tested','Sealed sample and repeated acoustic measurements'],['Drops folding cycles and ageing','Not physically tested','Manufactured samples and selected material grades']]
 table(d,['Check','Current record','Scope or missing input'],rows,[1.9,1.65,3.35])
 para(d,'An assembly sample holds the allocated spring space at 15 mm. An actual coil would expand when released, so a suitable compression fixture and real handling trial are still needed. The CAD does not model thread helices, nut installation tools or a verified retained connection between knob and pin. Clearance alone cannot establish a safe release control.')
 para(d,'V12 has six completed ideal band fixtures and two completed fork mesh comparisons. Those results stay labelled V12. V14 deliberately inherits the V12 band and cushion bodies through its construction script, but coincident Boolean component comparisons were not a reliable equivalence proof. No new six size V14 material qualification or complete assembly stress pass is claimed.')
 para(d,'One V14 calculation first stopped because its load face selection did not account for a 0.001 mm construction change. The selector was corrected against the saved surface bounds. A subsequent structural solve and a STEP export ran out of allocation space on the laptop. Those attempts are failures, not accepted results. Reruns use separate sequential processes; only completed and checked records appear as passes here.')
 f=O/'fork_mechanics_summary.json'
 if f.exists():
  summary=json.loads(f.read_text());new_page(d,'V14 Ideal fork fixture results')
  table(d,['Size','Fine displacement mm','Fine sampled stress MPa','Mesh comparison'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),f"{r['meshes'][-1]['weighted_load_direction_displacement_mm']:.4f}",f"{r['meshes'][-1]['max_von_mises_centroid_MPa']:.2f}",'Pass' if r['mesh_comparison_pass'] else 'Fail'] for r in summary['cases']],[1.5,1.65,1.65,2.1])
  para(d,'The right main fork receives the entire illustrative locking bore force with its pivot bores fixed. The cap and fasteners are excluded. This is an ideal component fixture with assumed modulus 2000 MPa and Poisson ratio 0.35. It does not solve the assembled bearing contact, cap screw preload, friction or a drop. The chosen comparison uses 5 percent changes in load direction displacement and sampled peak stress.')
  for r in summary['cases']:
   para(d,f"For {r['size'].replace('_',' ')}, the two mesh sizes are 2.0 and 1.5 mm. Load direction displacement changed by {100*r['displacement_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent and sampled peak stress by {100*r['sampled_peak_stress_mesh_change_fraction']:.2f} percent. Saved result arrays also passed checks of force balance, fixed displacement, positive element Jacobians, the equation residual and external work against strain energy.")
  para(d,'A numerical refinement pass establishes consistency of this fixture only. It cannot establish comfort, resistance to breakage, a material winner or superiority over market products. Final grades, production geometry and measured material behaviour remain required.')
 pack=O/'packing_summary.json'
 if pack.exists():
  packing=json.loads(pack.read_text());new_page(d,'V14 Folding size and carrying result')
  table(d,['Size','Folded box mm','Change from nominal box'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),' by '.join(f'{x:.1f}' for x in r['folded_box_mm']),f"{abs(r['reduction_percent']):.2f} percent "+('smaller' if r['reduction_percent']>=0 else 'larger')] for r in packing['sizes']],[1.5,3.3,2.1])
  para(d,'These are tight bounding boxes of the saved rigid CAD poses, including the new cap hardware and pull knobs. Child small improves by less than 1 percent. Child medium and large become about 1 to 1.5 percent larger. The child folding mechanism therefore fails our intended useful packing goal. Adult examples give about 12 to 23 percent reduction. None is a physical carrying case or transport survival test.')
  if (P/'documents/images/V14_folded_CAD.png').exists():
   new_page(d,'V14 Nominal and folded CAD')
   picture(d,'V14_folded_CAD','Saved V14 nominal surfaces shown with the recorded rigid folding transforms. Display scale is the same within each size row. Colours do not select materials.',6.2)
 para(d,'Folding stops, pinching and release force for individual users remain open. The child mechanism needs redesign or comparison with a simpler nonfolding version before claiming easy carrying. A collision free sampled path alone does not satisfy the portability objective.')
 para(d,'The nominal pin has only 0.05 mm radial clearance in its guide; the collar has 0.10 mm in the housing. These clearances need a capable process and checks for coatings, dirt, misalignment and wear. The pull knob bore currently matches the rod envelope exactly. That is not a modelled or qualified thread, anti loosening feature or pullout pass. Final retained knob and fastener specifications remain a design task.')
 para(d,'The digital review remains separate from product validation. The 70 material families are a register with limited reference calculations, not every material tested. We have no final supplier quote, measured Sony interface, manufactured prototype, matched competitor laboratory test or wearer study. V14 is not a manufacturing release.')
